<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Cofinimmo 1996 div shoots up.</title>
<headline>Belgian Cofinimmo 1996 div shoots up.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		165	     vs  76</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)	    194.12	  vs  89.41</p>
<p>    Cons profit			    1.247	   vs  n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Cofinimmo is a Belgian fixed capital real estate investment trust (Sicaf).  </p>
<p>Net asset value per share (in francs)</p>
<p>    - before appropriation	     3,988	   vs  3,853</p>
<p>    - after appropriation		3,794	   vs  3,764</p>
<p>NOTE - The value of the property portfolio estimated Winssinger &amp; Associates was 27.75 million francs. The rental occupancy rate was 90 percent. Consolidated shareholders' equity amounted to 19.22 million francs. Debt as a ratio of total assets stood at 31.73 percent on December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Cofinimmo said the increase in the dividend was mainly due to the group's change in status to Sicaf on April 1, 1996, affecting three quarters of accounts.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
